  "description": "This course covers instruction set architecture, including ARM and x86-64 instruction sets; memory hierarchy design with cache memory and virtual memory; pipelining techniques for RISC-V and x86 processors; CPU performance analysis using Amdahl's Law; parallel processing with SIMD instructions; system interconnects such as PCIe and USB; storage systems including SSDs and RAID configurations; and computer organization with FPGAs and embedded systems. Students will explore computer arithmetic, including floating-point operations and integer division; address translation using page tables and TLBs; and input/output mechanisms with DMA and interrupt handling. The course also covers computer organization and architecture standards such as IEEE 754 for floating-point arithmetic and ISO/IEC 2382 for terminology. Topics include CPU scheduling algorithms, memory management techniques, and system design for multi-core and distributed systems.",
